# Citation File Format 1.2.0. https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# `.zenodo.json` sits beside this file and it is the one Zenodo reads. Where both are present
# Zenodo uses `.zenodo.json` alone and ignores this file entirely
# (https://help.zenodo.org/docs/github/describe-software/), so `.zenodo.json` carries the whole
# record: title, description, creator with ORCID, licence, version, keywords and the related
# identifiers for the PyPI release and the GitHub tag. The two files hold the same facts in two
# vocabularies and are edited together. An edit made here and not there reaches a reader of this
# repository and never reaches the archive.
#
# `doi` is absent on purpose. It is known only once a GitHub Release has been archived by Zenodo,
# and a placeholder would be an invalid value rather than a missing one. Add the VERSION doi, not
# the concept doi: a verdict is the output of one rule set, so a citation that does not name the
# version has not said which instrument produced its numbers.
#
# `date-released` is the date of the CHANGELOG section this version ships under, and it moves when
# the version does.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the specific version you ran."
type: software
title: langaccess
abstract: >-
  langaccess audits the language accessibility of a website. The tool renders the site in a
  headless browser and classifies, for each language present, the access provided: English-only
  content, a machine-translation widget, or text authored by the site itself. Each classification
  is returned with its supporting evidence, the URL and quoted text that decided it, and the
  numbered classification rules that were applied.
authors:
  - family-names: Yoo
    given-names: Nari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8467-7048"
    email: nariyoo@umich.edu
    affiliation: University of Michigan School of Social Work
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
repository-code: "https://github.com/nariyoo/langaccess"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-SA-3.0
keywords:
  - language access
  - multilingual
  - website audit
  - machine translation
  - limited English proficiency
  - health equity
  - web measurement
